# Data model

Canonical shape (see `src/core` / `openspec/specs/book-core/`): `book.json` as book → spreads → frames, plus assets map and ordered gallery of asset ids. Pages are derived from spreads — do not store `pages[]` or slots.

- Current `schemaVersion` is 2. Asset map values are records with optional `sourceRootId`, `relativePath`, `byteSize`, `mtimeMs`, `contentHash` (all omitted until identity/import fills them).
- Physical units are millimeters; crop is `{ zoom ≥ 1, center }` in normalized source space.
- Validate load boundaries with Zod (`parseBook`); refuse newer `schemaVersion`; migrate supported older versions.
- Prefer immutable updates with structural sharing (`updateSpread` / `updateFrame`).
- Do not store `File` / `Blob` / handles in the document — assets are ids only.
- Do not invent parallel schemas without an OpenSpec change.
